<title>USA: BioSpecifics says treatment promising.</title>
<headline>BioSpecifics says treatment promising.</headline>
<dateline>LYNBROOK, N.Y. 1997-02-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>BioSpecifics Technologies Corp said on Tuesday its new treatment for keloids and hypertrophic scars showed promising preliminary results in the early phases of testing.</p>
<p>A report presented at the annual International Burn Foundation conference in Maui, Hawaii, said positive results were achieved during a Phase 1 study of BioSpecifics' purified enzyme Collagenase, the company said.</p>
<p>The product digests collagen, the material that forms the keloid or hypertrophic scar.</p>
<p>	  ((-- New York Newsdesk 212 859-1610))</p>
